# The context of `apps/selfhost/Dockerfile` is the whole workspace, so this keeps out what the image builds for itself
# and what must never be in a layer.

# Installed and built inside the image, for its own platform.
**/node_modules
**/build
**/.svelte-kit
**/dist
.wrangler
**/.wrangler

# A record, a key file or a copy on this machine is somebody's data, never the image's. `apps/selfhost/src/baked.ts`
# holds the same list: the build stops, and the image refuses to start, if any of these got in some other way.
# A backup folder holds the key file, the records and each record's inbound mail token, so it is kept out whole.
**/backups
**/braindog-backups
**/braindog-2*
**/inbound.token
**/claim-link
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite-*
**/*.brain
**/*.brainl
**/*.brainl.age
**/kek
**/kek.prev
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.dev.vars

# History, screenshots and logs the server never reads.
.git
shots
**/*.log
